menu "RMT-UART"
    config RU_FLT_MODE
        int "Filter Mode (0=Dis, 1=HW, 2=SW, 3=Both)"
        range 0 3
        default 2
        help
            Basic SW logic seems more resilient and predictable than HW for UART signals.
            Both and Disabled are only meant for testing.
    config RU_SLOW_EDGE
        bool "Slow edge compensation (recommended)"
        default y
        help
            Add a non-cumulative rounding value to each run length instead of loosening the basePeriod
            This can work well when most of the error comes from edge transitions (on by default)
endmenu
